---
description: Colour contrast — dark text on light surfaces, light text on dark
alwaysApply: true
---

# Contrast rule

- **Light / bright backgrounds** (including solid `--yellow` `#ffd700`): use dark text via `--ink-on-yellow` (or dark `--ink` in light theme). Never put light-grey / `--ink-soft` / dark-theme `--ink` on yellow.
- **Dark backgrounds** (page `--bg`, dark `--yellow-wash`): use light text (`--ink` in dark theme).
- Solid yellow accents stay bright in both themes — always pair with `--ink-on-yellow`, not theme `--ink`.
- Soft wash (`--yellow-wash`) follows the theme (pale in light, deep in dark) — pair with theme `--ink`, not a fixed light grey.
